# Use case: machine learning and geostatistics for Baltimore house prices

## Setup

> Run this notebook from a checkout of Geostatex (it reads the data under `notebooks/data`):
>
> ```
> livebook server notebooks/baltimore_ml_case.livemd
> ```
>
> or headlessly, to check that every cell works:
>
> ```
> elixir scripts/run_livemd.exs notebooks/baltimore_ml_case.livemd
> ```
>
> Spanish version: `notebooks/es/caso_ml_baltimore.livemd`.
>
> The models train on Nx's pure-Elixir backend, so the cross-validation of section 3 takes a few
> minutes; adding `{:exla, ...}` and `Nx.global_default_backend(EXLA.Backend)` makes it faster.

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:geostatex, path: Path.join(__DIR__, "..")},
  # A checkout builds the NIF from source, which needs Rustler and a Rust toolchain.
  {:rustler, "~> 0.38", runtime: false},
  {:geoframe, "~> 0.3.3"},
  {:explorer, "~> 0.13"},
